            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="TAY04" sex="2">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Susannah</forename>
                        <surname>Taylor</surname>
                        <addName>née Cook</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1755-03-29">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1823-06-04"/>
                    <occupation>writer</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Susannah was a prominent member of radical circles in Norwich.  She was the wife of <persName key="TAY02">John Taylor </persName> of Norwich 
     and mother of a number of children who also appear in the diary. She was a celebrated conversationalist and there is an account 
     of her in Janet Ross’s 1888 <title>Three Generations of       Englishwomen</title>.</p>
                        <p>Instances of 'Susan Taylor' and 'Mrs Taylor' have been identified as Susannah; please see discussion under <persName key="TAY01">John Taylor</persName>.</p>
                        <p>Godwin records her death.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS">MS. Abinger c. 12, fol. 20: 10 March 1818.</bibl>
                    <bibl type="MS">MS. Abinger c. 12, fols. 98-9: 9 March 1821.</bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">David Chandler, <title>Norwich Literature, 1788-97: A Critical Survey</title> (unpub. Oxford D.Phil. thesis, 1997)</bibl>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
